FFmpeg's DASH demuxer calls xmlCleanupParser() after every manifest it parses. libxml2 documents that function as
freeing the state of the whole process, for a time when no thread is parsing: a parse going on in another thread (or in
another library of the process, as Foundation's XMLParser) crashes in the table of character encodings it frees.
Upstream (master and release/9.0, libavformat/dashdec.c) still has the call. Applied by scripts/build_dependencies.sh
to FFmpeg 9.0.2; the state libxml2 keeps is freed at exit.

--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -1431,7 +1431,8 @@
 cleanup:
         /*free the document */
         xmlFreeDoc(doc);
-        xmlCleanupParser();
+        /* Not xmlCleanupParser(): it frees libxml2's state for the whole process, and a parse going on in another
+         * thread (or in another library) crashes on it. The state is freed at exit. */
         xmlFreeNode(mpd_baseurl_node);
     }
 
